<title>CROATIA: Croatia c.bank injects 189.3 mln kuna repo funds.</title>
<headline>Croatia c.bank injects 189.3 mln kuna repo funds.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Croatia's central bank said it injected 189.3 million kuna into the banking system on Friday through a repo deal.</p>
<p>It bought from nine commercial banks outstanding 35- and 91-day liquidity bills and treasury bills nominally worth 190.6 million kuna.</p>
<p>The deal expires on May 21. The bills will be due for repurchase at a weighted rate of 9.41 percent, the bank said.</p>
<p>-- Davor Huic, Zagreb Newsroom, 385-1-4557075</p>
</text>
